;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>270</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> causing the compression of the gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>217</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>167</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math>. The change in internal energy of the process, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>'</mo></math>&nbsp;is _____.</p><p>[nearest integer]</p><p>(Given: atomic mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;Molar heat capacity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "42a1d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948c6"}, {"id": "723921", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948c7"}, {"id": "f19585", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948c8"}, {"id": "af8daa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948c9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "According to the following figure, the magnitude of the enthalpy change of the reaction<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />is equal to __________ . (Integer answer)<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8899b670-d7a1-4521-83f3-25f9c1626537-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 343px; height: 230px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "927f60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948cb"}, {"id": "44b52b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948cc"}, {"id": "b4cacf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948cd"}, {"id": "843de7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948cf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "The enthalpy of formation of ethane \\(\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_6\\right)\\) from ethylene by addition of hydrogen where the bond-energies of \\(\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{H}\\) are \\(414 \\mathrm{~kJ}, 347 \\mathrm{~kJ}, 615 \\mathrm{~kJ}\\) and \\(435 \\mathrm{~kJ}\\) respectively is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\mathrm{kJ}\\)"}, "options": [{"id": "bf8597", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d0"}, {"id": "f622fe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d1"}, {"id": "a44fa8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d2"}, {"id": "a95bd0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "When 2 litre of ideal gas expands isothermally into vacuum to a total volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> litre, the change in internal energy is _____&nbsp;J. (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "b70e52", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d5"}, {"id": "3c86c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d6"}, {"id": "ed3f3a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d7"}, {"id": "dfb8a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948d9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "<p>Solid fuel used in rocket is a mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math>&nbsp;(in ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>). The heat evolved <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>)</mo></math> per gram of the mixture is _____ (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>840</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AI</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>27</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6ae247", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948da"}, {"id": "eccf3a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948db"}, {"id": "e0a98d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948dc"}, {"id": "126060", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948dd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948de", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6176f3ee6581241c7072a758"], "question": {"text": "Combustion of 1 mole of benzene is expressed at\n\\(\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6(\\mathrm{l})+\\frac{15}{2} \\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 6 \\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+3 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l}) \\text {. }\\)\nThe standard enthalpy of combustion of \\(2 \\mathrm{~mol}\\) of benzene is \\(-^{\\prime} x^{\\prime} \\mathrm{kJ}\\).\n\\(x=\\) ______\nGiven:\n1. standard Enthalpy of formation of \\(1 \\mathrm{~mol}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6(\\mathrm{l})\\), for the reaction \\(6 \\mathrm{C}\\) (graphite) \\(+3 \\mathrm{H}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6(\\mathrm{l})\\) is \\(48.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\).\n2. Standard Enthalpy of formation of \\(1 \\mathrm{~mol}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})\\), for the reaction \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) (graphite) \\(+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})\\) is \\(-393.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\).\n3. Standard and Enthalpy of formation of \\(1 \\mathrm{~mol}\\) of \\(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l})\\), for the reaction \\(\\mathrm{H}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l})\\) is \\(-286 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\)."}, "options": [{"id": "562534", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948df"}, {"id": "a9c983", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e0"}, {"id": "82418c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e1"}, {"id": "8323aa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6117b5e4478ae845c43c5e1c"], "question": {"text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the enthalpy of fusion of a solid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the enthalpy of vaporisation of the liquid&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The enthalpy of sublimation of the substance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is&nbsp;______. (in nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "0b8772", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e4"}, {"id": "974c85", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e5"}, {"id": "ed56ed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e6"}, {"id": "9741c0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6162fb8c6ed13040ec8502c6"], "question": {"text": "When equal volume of \\(1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{HCl}\\) and \\(1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4\\) are separately neutralised by excess volume of \\(1 \\mathrm{M}\\) \\(\\mathrm{NaOH}\\) solution. \\(x\\) and \\(y \\mathrm{~kJ}\\) of heat is liberated respectively. The value of \\(y / x\\) is _______"}, "options": [{"id": "2bf2fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948e9"}, {"id": "03c244", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ea"}, {"id": "fc5f7c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948eb"}, {"id": "31d441", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ed", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6117b64e478ae845c43c6873"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>AB</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are diatomic molecules. If the bond enthalpies of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> are in the ratio<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the bond enthalpy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_________kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c15494", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ee"}, {"id": "fbad92", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ef"}, {"id": "e7e390", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f0"}, {"id": "b8a9a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>59</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p><p>The enthalpy change for the above reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mo>-</mo></mfenced></math>____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(nearest integer)</p><p>(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) .</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8ca538", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f3"}, {"id": "d8de40", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f4"}, {"id": "2eea11", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f5"}, {"id": "a546b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "<p>The standard enthalpies of formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CaO</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1675</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>635</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>For the reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>CaO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Al</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>Ca</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;the standard&nbsp;reaction enthalpy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "045d6c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f8"}, {"id": "e2980f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948f9"}, {"id": "63f3a0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948fa"}, {"id": "305987", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948fc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "<p>For complete combustion of methanol</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;the amount of heat produced as measured by bomb calorimeter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>726</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The enthalpy of combustion for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />integer)<br />(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b33b49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948fd"}, {"id": "237f01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948fe"}, {"id": "f3ab2c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d92948ff"}, {"id": "9c0b56", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294900"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294901", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6176f3ee6581241c7072a758"], "question": {"text": "<p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, the enthalpy of the following processes are given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>OH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>242</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>436</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>249</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>What would be the value of X&nbsp;for the following reaction? (Nearest integer)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>OH</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvarian