 "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294916"}, {"id": "0acf72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294917"}, {"id": "dd3e68", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294918"}, {"id": "ea4e0e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294919"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "<p>Standard enthalpy of vapourisation for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Heat required for vapourisation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>284</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> at constant temperature is __________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>. (Given molar mass in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>gmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>)</p><p>Round off your answer to the nearest integer.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cd8734", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491b"}, {"id": "dbb1e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491c"}, {"id": "c6b160", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491d"}, {"id": "abf787", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d929491f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "<p>The average <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> bond energy in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math> is _. (Rounded off to the nearest integer)</p><p>[Given : The values of standard enthalpy of formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1100</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>275</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively.]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "bc4da1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294920"}, {"id": "920682", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294921"}, {"id": "524c2a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294922"}, {"id": "9b44ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294923"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294924", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "For complete combustion of ethene,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />the amount of heat produced as measured in bomb calorimeter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1406</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T&#916;S</mi></math> needed to reach equilibrium is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)<br />Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "a2466d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294925"}, {"id": "e2cbb3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294926"}, {"id": "ef97e0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294927"}, {"id": "f53f32", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f852ee0e063d9294928"}], "questionLab